# LF for source code, also on Windows checkouts: git hooks run under sh (Git for Windows), and line-based
# checks (security.test.ts, guard-diff) must see the same text on every OS.
# Deliberately not repo-wide: data/ and test fixtures keep their bytes (some corpus files use CRLF on purpose).
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
# The corpus is hashed in FREEZE.sha256: never convert line endings in it, even with core.autocrlf=true
# (otherwise PDFs, JSON gold and the CRLF .txt uploads change bytes on a Windows checkout).
data/synthetic_sops/** -text
data/synthetic_sops/**/*.py text eol=lf
